#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Feedcairn demo AI CLI. Reads the prompt from stdin and prints a deterministic briefing.
# Demo only: point Settings → command at this file to test the AI panel without any account. Never put it on PATH.
set -euo pipefail
prompt="$(cat || true)"
title="$(printf '%s\n' "$prompt" | awk -F'Title: ' '/Title: /{print $2; exit}')"
provider="$(basename "$0")"
cat <<EOF
[Feedcairn stub · ${provider}]

This is local demo output. Replace this binary with a real CLI, or set Settings → ${provider} command to your tool.

$(if [ -n "${title}" ]; then echo "Article: ${title}"; fi)

## Takeaways
- The model would normally summarize the article you selected.
- Feedcairn sent the prompt on stdin (see README for the invocation shape).
- No API keys are stored in the app; your CLI owns credentials.

## Why it matters
A working CLI on PATH is all Feedcairn needs. Keep using this stub in CI or when you want a guaranteed response.

--- prompt excerpt ---
$(printf '%s' "$prompt" | head -c 400)
EOF
